# HyperNexus — Meta model wiring for Claude Code (REFERENCE SNIPPET, no secrets inside).
# =============================================================================
# Model: muse-spark-1.3-contributor via the HyperNexus kernel's Anthropic shim
# (go/internal/httpapi/anthropic_compat.go: POST /v1/messages, GET /v1/models).
#
# NATIVE PATH (no minting, no key handling): the kernel reads the pi Meta OAuth
# identity ITSELF per request (~/.pi/agent/auth.json -> meta.refresh/access) and
# forwards to https://api.meta.ai/v1/chat/completions. Pi owns OAuth refresh,
# so the identity auto-renews; nothing is stored anywhere in Claude config.
#
#   ~/.claude/settings.json:
#     { "env": {
+#         "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:7778",
+#         "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "hypernexus-local",
+#         "ANTHROPIC_MODEL": "muse-spark-1.3-contributor" } }
+#
+# Then:  claude --plugin-dir <path-to>/plugin/hypernexus "your prompt"
+# or:    .\use-meta-model.ps1 "your prompt"   (mints a fresh override key per run)
+#
+# OVERRIDE PATH (optional): META_MUSE_API_KEY env — when set, the kernel uses it
+# instead of the pi identity. Minted fresh per run via bin/meta-muse-key.mjs
+# (pi identity .meta.refresh -> POST https://api.meta.ai/muse-code/key).
+# Mint helper probe: node bin/meta-muse-key.mjs --check   (expect: mint OK)
+#
+# WHY NOT .meta.access directly: auth.json .meta.access is a SHORT-LIVED token
+# (minutes). The durable pattern mints a Model API key from the identity
+# .meta.refresh (same as Droid apiKeyHelper + crush startup mint) — or skips
+# minting entirely and lets the kernel read pi's store per request.
+#
+# VERIFY: node bin/meta-muse-key.mjs --check
+#         curl -s http://127.0.0.1:7778/v1/models
+#         claude --plugin-dir plugin/hypernexus -p --model muse-spark-1.3-contributor "reply with exactly: CLAUDE_META_OK"
+#
+# SECURITY: never paste a minted key into settings.json (dies in ~24h) and never
+# commit one. Pi owns refresh; this file carries no credential.
